## 3. What the fetch script does to each dataset

| Dataset | Preparation |
|---|---|
| Roche66k | one table of 72,142 reactions → keep rows whose `output_column` has a `"<time> h at <temperature> °C"` stage (first stage) → 51,275 rows → split by reaction type (7 single + one BH ∪ SM union); counts 3,917 / 14,191 / 9,946 / 3,100 / 2,112 / 2,095 / 1,251 / 24,137 |
| DoyleHTE | 4,599 rows (16 substrates × 24 additives) → drop substrate `none` and the four additives that do not cover the panel → complete 15 × 20 grid, 3,600 rows |
| Summit | skip the `TYPE` row of each case file, stack the four Reizman cases (385 rows), add `substrate_type` |
| rxn_yields | xlsx → CSV, column names unchanged (5,760 rows × 16 columns) |
| AI_RCP, bh-hte-ood | used as published |

A different cut, a missing step or the raw files give different row counts, and
therefore different Table 1 entries, ceilings and R² values.
